// The reach of the mass media (`media`, `game::Switches::media`; docs/politics.pt-BR.md, "Mídia",
// slice 1, owner's decision MD1: reach measured from what people buy and read, never a fixed
// historical series). Read only with the switch on.
//
// DESIGN VALUES, not from a source (the stocks they make are compared with the UNESCO and ITU
// series in the doc, as a check, not a target):
// - a tenth of the households' consumer electronics are sets for the media (the rest is the other
//   appliances);
// - a radio set costs 0.6 units of consumer electronics (a lot of $1,000 of 2011: a 1930 set of
//   some $50, about $700 today), lasts 10 years; a television set 2 units, 10 years; an internet
//   user 1 unit (the device and the line), 5 years;
// - the households' purchases of the good split among the open media: radio alone takes all;
//   with television, 30 % radio and 70 % television; with the web, 10 %, 40 % and 50 %;
// - a literate person buys at most 0.65 daily copies, half of that at a GDP per head of 15,000
//   (1925 base prices); the stock closes a tenth of the gap a year;
// - a copy is read by 2.5 people, a set reaches 3.5 (a household), a user is one person.
(
    electronics: "consumer_electronics",
    sets_share: 0.1,
    sets: [
        ("radio", 0.6, 10),
        ("television", 2.0, 10),
        ("world_wide_web", 1.0, 5),
    ],
    split: [
        [1.0, 0.0, 0.0],
        [0.3, 0.7, 0.0],
        [0.1, 0.4, 0.5],
    ],
    copies_per_literate: 0.65,
    copies_half_income: 15000.0,
    news_pace: 0.1,
    people_per_unit: [2.5, 3.5, 3.5, 1.0],
    // What the media do (slice 2, in draft: the owner's MD2, MD3 and MD6 at the recommended
    // answer). DESIGN VALUES, per mille: (a movement grows 50 % faster at full free reach; 50 %
    // slower at full official reach, and what it loses feeds the movement for a change of regime;
    // the official media add 100 to the war's support target at full official reach; the free
    // media make the support move 50 % faster at full free reach; full internet access takes 80 %
    // of the censorship's force).
    effects: Some((500, 500, 100, 500, 800)),
)
